+        standard deduction was taken for 2024) has no 2024 line 7 to read.'
+      readings:
+      - Ask only for an amount on line 7 of a 2024 Form 4952; such a filer answers No and enters no carryforward.
+      - Use the amount a 2024 Form 4952 would have shown on line 7 had one been completed (the carryforward, treated as 2024
+        investment interest, less the part the 2024 net investment income could have absorbed).
+      - Use line 7 of the latest Form 4952 filed.
+      chosen: The first (f4952.carryover asks only about a 2024 Form 4952), until the owner rules on a refusing question for
+        this case.
+      reason: 'Pub. 550: "You can carry over the amount of investment interest you could not deduct because of this limit to
+        the next tax year. The interest carried over is treated as investment interest paid or accrued in that next year."
+        The third reading carries the whole earlier amount past a year whose net investment income could have absorbed it,
